A||||20||87FieroGTx||best way to change alternator??????||||5||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||08-29-2001||07:24 PM||||Would any one know a way to change out an alternator with out a lift &gt;? Is it posible if so how?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||08-29-2001||07:36 PM||||It is possible without a lift.  <P>1.Make sure to  unhook the negative battery terminal first!!!  <P>2.Jack up the car and look under.  You will probably have to remove the right rear tire.  <P>3.Unplug the connector that plugs into the back of the alternator, and remove the positive wire that is back there too.  Cant remember what size nut it is that holds it on....   <P>4.Take off your engines belt.  <P>5.Remove the 2 bolts that hold it on (one long one on bottom and shorter one on the top) and lower it out the bottom.  <P>6.Remove the alternator from the engine compartment.  It is hard to get it out of the engine compartment.  I always have to yank it out from the right rear tire area.  It takes time but you should find a way to get it out.  <P>7.Install the new one the oppisite of removal. <P>Sorry..these are not the clearest of instructions...i am really tired.  It has been a long day.  I hope they help some.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Let me know how it turns out!  Time for a nap for me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||08-29-2001||07:36 PM||||Well, ummm, huhh, uh, yeah, what he said, I thiiiink..<P>Would help if we knew engine, trans, year, etc. <P>Why would a Fiero owner need a lift to change an alt? You need no lift.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||08-29-2001||09:17 PM||||The easiest way is to drive or tow the car to a Pontiac dealer and have them do it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||08-29-2001||09:26 PM||||I just bought a new alt. and paid a local mechanic $30 to put it in.  He's had a few Fiero's himself, so I knew he had an idea of what he was doing. Did a great job too.  I'll give him a plug here too.....<BR>Merril & Sons, In Jefferson WI.  Right on the main drag.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||08-29-2001||09:30 PM||||not again.   Do you do it from the top or do you do it from the bottem. This is the question????????<P>I always do it from the top!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||10:00 PM||||I myself like to switch on top for awhile then Ilike to do it from the bottom I defeinetly dont like that bendind over part I really hate that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>And lar you beat me out with your response,no snuzzin aroud here <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT-maniac||08-29-2001||11:14 PM||||Well the last time I changed mine I drove the car just up on the edge of the sidewalk in front of my house. Had lots of room underneath then and didn't need any jack or anything. Then I just dropped it out the bottom, one of the easier jobs to do on a fiero. At least with a V6 and a 4 speed.  ||||reg||7
Z||000008||Her86GT||08-29-2001||11:42 PM||||My mechanic did me. . oh, I mean MINE from the top. . .less than half an hour and he was done.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Needed a new regulator (voltage)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar2sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||08-29-2001||11:43 PM||||I have an 85SE v-6 4spd and an 85gt auto.  The 4spd one is pretty easy to get out.<P>On the auto trans I have to take the cooling fan tubes off the rear bulkhead (trunk wall) and the bracket that mounts the dogbone to the rear head.  Then the alternator comes out the top.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fiero*101||08-29-2001||11:47 PM||||ok i want to know how in the HELL you guys took the Alt out of the top of the v6<P>I just changed mine about a month ago and i had to take off the rear right wheel to get to it and it was a pain to do it by my self but i did it but the stupid tention bolt worked its self loose last night and now its squealing. So i have to get back under it and tighten it<P>Any have any idea how i keep the tention bolt tight so this does not happen again?<P><BR>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000011||GT-maniac||08-30-2001||02:52 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Fiero*101:<BR>[B]ok i want to know how in the HELL you guys took the Alt out of the top of the v6<P>I just changed mine about a month ago and i had to take off the rear right wheel to get to it and it was a pain to do it by my self but i did it but the stupid tention bolt worked its self loose last night and now its squealing. So i have to get back under it and tighten it<P>Any have any idea how i keep the tention bolt tight so this does not happen again?<P><BR>You have to use some kind of bar ( a tire iron works well ) to apply tension to the belt by prying against the alternator. Then while your applying tension with one hand tighten up the tension bolt with the other hand. Far easier to do this from below. If you've done it right you should have about 3/4 inch of play when you push down on the belt with a finger.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||87FieroGTx||08-31-2001||12:20 AM|||| Thx for all the Info, My car is a 85 GT Auto.<P> Ok.. So I should jack up the rear end, Take off the rear right Tire, Take the belt off, Take the Alternator off, put the new one on, Belt on, Tire on And thats it?<P>||||reg||1
