Z||000015||johnmac||09-01-2001||03:42 PM||||Taking it off from the bottom on a V6 Automatic is ALMOST IMPOSSIBLE!  PERIOD.<P>I tried over and over and was forced to remove the tie rod, muffler and suspension from the bottom to get it out.<P>I am going from the TOP next time!<P>This is reality!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000016||PBJ||09-01-2001||07:39 PM||||Like I said, always from the top.||||reg||1
Z||000017||XDrewX||09-01-2001||08:47 PM||||I have not had to change my alt. YET!!!<BR>But i have a v6 Automatic.  For all the people who say "out the top" PLEASE elaborate. <P>Thank You||||reg||1
Z||000018||PBJ||09-02-2001||07:30 PM||||ok, out the top. here is how I did it.<P>one was a 86 2m6 4spd no a/c<BR>other done twice now is a 86 GT auto with a/c.<P>go under car and remove bolt from alt for adjuster bracket.<P>the rest is from the top untill you have the alt back in and ready to tighten alt belt.<P>remove dog bone and bracket.<BR>remove heat shield off the back of the alt.<BR>remove forced air ducting from trunk wall<BR>remove wires from alt.<BR>remove alt from brackets.<BR>remove upper alt bracket completely, this includes the lower bolt with 18mm head-you may have trouble re-installing this bolt if mtr mount bracket is not tight cause bolt is also one of the two frt mtr mount bolt.<BR>now alt should come up out of top.<BR>may need pry bar to rock engine slightly if alt gets hung up.<P>sorry if I forgot any thing its been a few months now.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||PBJ||09-02-2001||07:33 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012589.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012589.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||starfighter007@msn.com||09-02-2001||07:48 PM||||Hey guys this sound pretty serious. I changed mine out a few months back I have a v-6 5 speed and I dont recall any problems However I dont remember if I acyually tok it out from the top or the bottom .are the automatics that differant that it is impossible to remove from the bottom? And I hope that by my ignorance to this obvious problem let me get lucky.Please post how this turns out for you goodluck.||||reg||1
